<title>UK: Allied Colloids buys Imdex chemicals unit.</title>
<headline>Allied Colloids buys Imdex chemicals unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial chemicals firm Allied Colloids Group Plc said on Thursday it has agreed to buy Imdex Chemicals, a unit of Australia's Imdex NL, for around 13.5 million Australian dollars (6.7 million stg) in cash.</p>
<p>Imdex Chemicals manufactures a range of anionic, nonionic and cationic polymers used primarily in mining and industrial processing. It operates from Kwinana, Western Australia and is well-positioned to supply the Asia-Pacific economies.</p>
<p>Allied Colloids said the acquisition should be completed by the end of the month.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
